hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"23600","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, al-Mubarak narrated to us, al-Hasan narrated to us that an old man from Banu Salit informed him, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to speak to him about something suffered by us in the pre-Islamic period, and he was sitting with a circle surrounding him, relating to the people, wearing a thick cotton lower garment. The first thing I heard him say, while pointing with his two fingers: The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim; he does not wrong him nor forsake him. Piety is here, piety is here, meaning in the heart."
"23601","Umar ibn Sa'd Abu Dawud al-Hafari narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ya'ni Ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, Sa'd ibn Tariq narrated to me from Bilal ibn Yahya from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: A Bedouin informed me that he heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: I fear nothing for Quraysh except themselves. I said: What is with them? He said: Covetous and quarrelsome, and if your life is prolonged you will see them tempting the people until you see the people among them like sheep between two watering troughs, to this one at one time and to this one at another time."
"23602","Al-Zubayri narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us from Simak from Ma'bad ibn Qays from Abdullah ibn Umayr or Umayrah, he said: The husband of the daughter of Abu Lahab narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to us when I married the daughter of Abu Lahab, and he said: Is there any entertainment?"
"23603","Abu Amir narrated to us, Ali narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, Hayyah al-Tamimi narrated to us that his father informed him that he heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: There is nothing in al-hamah, and the evil eye is true, and the truest of foreboding is al-fa'l."
"23604","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Aban and Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us from Yahya from Abu Ja'far from Ata ibn Yasar from one of the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: While a man was praying trailing his izar, the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Go and perform ablution. He went and performed ablution, then he came, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Go and perform ablution. He went and performed ablution, then he came, and they said: O Messenger of Allah, why did you order him to perform ablution then you said nothing to him? He said: He was praying while trailing his izar, and Allah does not accept the prayer of a servant who trails his izar."
